  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.new` has two obligations: `ValidationCache::new()` creates an empty cache, and that cache has no agent. `ValidationCache` has only two fields, `outlines` and `agent`.\n\n- **Unit test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#mod[tests]/fn[new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent]` calls `ValidationCache::new()`. It asserts that `outlines` is empty and that `agent.is_none()`. That covers both fields, so it covers both obligations.\n- **Integration test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path]` also carries a `{test}` reference to this requirement. It builds a cache with `new()`. Its first `OutlineContent::from_path` call fails because the file doesn't exist yet. That shows the new cache starts without files. The test is mainly about other requirements, but it is consistent with this one.\n\nI found no other distinct modes or boundaries in the text. The exact signature `pub fn new() -> Self` is a compile-time property and needs no runtime test. I found no gaps.",
